14. METHOD 12: QUERY PARAMETERS
============================================================

Query parameters are commonly used for filtering and searching.


ROUTE:

Route::get('/employees', [EmployeeController::class, 'index'])
    ->name('employees.index');


BLADE:

<a href="{{ route('employees.index', [
    'department_id' => 2,
    'status' => 'active',
    'sort' => 'name',
]) }}">
    View Active Employees
</a>


GENERATED URL:

/employees?department_id=2&status=active&sort=name


CONTROLLER:

$departmentId = $request->query('department_id');

$status = $request->query('status');

$sort = $request->query('sort');


ROUTE PARAMETER:

/employees/5

Route:

Route::get('/employees/{employee}', ...);

The value 5 is a route parameter.


QUERY PARAMETER:

/employees?department_id=2

Route:

Route::get('/employees', ...);

The department_id value is a query parameter.


DIFFERENCE:

Route parameters:
    Identify a resource or form part of the URL structure.

Query parameters:
    Commonly specify filters, search terms, sorting, and options.

