16. METHOD 14: REDIRECT USING to_route()
============================================================

The to_route() helper redirects the browser to a named route.

EXAMPLE:

public function store(Request $request)
{
    // Validate and save the employee.

    return to_route('employees.index');
}


REDIRECT WITH A PARAMETER:

return to_route('employees.show', [
    'employee' => $employee->id,
]);


REDIRECT WITH A FLASH MESSAGE:

return to_route('employees.index')
    ->with('success', 'Employee created successfully.');


DISPLAY THE MESSAGE IN BLADE:

@if (session('success'))

    <div class="alert alert-success">
        {{ session('success') }}
    </div>

@endif


ALTERNATIVE:

return redirect()->route('employees.index');


DIFFERENCE:

route('employees.index')
    Generates a URL.

to_route('employees.index')
    Returns a redirect response to a named route.

Use route() in Blade links and form actions.

Use to_route() in controllers when redirecting after an operation.

