17. METHOD 15: old() AND @error
============================================================

These helpers are useful when form validation fails.


BLADE:

<form action="{{ route('employees.store') }}" method="POST">

    @csrf

    <label for="name">Name</label>

    <input
        type="text"
        id="name"
        name="name"
        value="{{ old('name') }}"
    >

    @error('name')
        <p class="error">{{ $message }}</p>
    @enderror

    <button type="submit">Save</button>

</form>


old('name')

    Retrieves the previous submitted value, typically flashed after a validation failure.

@error('name')

    Displays the validation error associated with the name field.


EDIT FORM:

<input
    type="text"
    name="name"
    value="{{ old('name', $employee->name) }}"
>


The first argument is the input field name.

The second argument is the default value.

If an old submitted value exists, it is displayed. Otherwise, the employee's saved name is displayed.

