21. METHOD 19: API ROUTES
============================================================

Laravel applications can have browser routes and API routes.

WEB:

routes/web.php

    Browser-facing routes.
    Commonly uses session authentication and Blade views.


API:

routes/api.php

    API endpoints.
    Commonly returns JSON for mobile applications and other API clients.


EXAMPLE API ROUTE:

Route::get('/employees', [EmployeeApiController::class, 'index'])
    ->name('api.employees.index');


BLADE LINK:

<a href="{{ route('api.employees.index') }}">
    Employee API
</a>


An API route typically returns JSON rather than a Blade page.

In Laravel 12, API routing may need to be installed and configured if routes/api.php does not exist.

For applications supporting both a website and a mobile app, keep web controllers and API controllers separate while reusing shared business logic through services.

