============================================================
30. MOST IMPORTANT CONCEPTS
============================================================

CONCEPT 1: GENERATE A URL

{{ route('employees.show', $employee) }}

This generates a URL.


CONCEPT 2: NAVIGATE TO A URL

<a href="{{ route('employees.show', $employee) }}">
    View Employee
</a>

The browser sends a GET request when the user clicks the link.


CONCEPT 3: SUBMIT DATA TO A ROUTE

<form action="{{ route('employees.store') }}" method="POST">

    @csrf

    <input type="text" name="name">

    <button type="submit">Save</button>

</form>

The browser sends the submitted form data to the route.


CONCEPT 4: REDIRECT THE BROWSER

return to_route('employees.show', $employee);

The controller returns a redirect response.


CONCEPT 5: PASS A ROUTE PARAMETER

route('employees.show', $employee)

The employee identifies the record associated with the route.


CONCEPT 6: PASS A QUERY PARAMETER

route('employees.index', ['search' => 'Gaurav'])

Generates a URL similar to:

/employees?search=Gaurav


CONCEPT 7: RECEIVE FORM DATA

$request->input('name');

The controller reads the submitted input.


CONCEPT 8: RECEIVE QUERY PARAMETERS

$request->query('search');

The controller reads a query-string value.


CONCEPT 9: PROTECT A WEB FORM

@csrf

Adds the CSRF token to a normal session-based web form.


CONCEPT 10: USE PUT, PATCH, OR DELETE

@method('PUT')

@method('PATCH')

@method('DELETE')

Laravel recognizes the intended HTTP method through method spoofing.


