FINAL RULE:

Use route() to generate URLs for named routes.

Use href for navigation links.

Use form action to specify where a form submits.

Use GET for navigation and retrieving filtered data.

Use POST to create records.

Use PUT or PATCH to update records.

Use DELETE to delete records.

Use @csrf for normal session-based web forms.

Use @method() when submitting PUT, PATCH, or DELETE through an HTML form.

Use to_route() when redirecting from a controller.

Use request()->query() to read query-string values.

Use $request->input() to read submitted request input.

Always validate input and enforce authorization on the server.
